# Execution Style

The user pays per request, not per token. Optimize for fewer requests, not fewer tokens.

## Rules

- Maximize work done in each request. Do not stop early or make partial deliveries.
- If you have questions, collect ALL of them and present them in a single batch. Never stop to ask one question at a time.
- Use as many tokens as needed within a single request. Token count is not a concern.
- Do not split work across multiple responses when it can be done in one.
- If a task has multiple steps, complete all steps before returning.
- Use parallel tool calls whenever possible to speed up execution.
- When creating multiple files, create them all in the same response.
- Reasonable execution time is expected — do not take excessively long, but thoroughness beats speed.

## Document Language

- Documents follow the language of the request. If asked in Portuguese, generate in Portuguese. If in English, in English.
- Code output (variable names, function names, comments) is always in English regardless of document language.
